{% extends 'config/maintenance/_layout.html.twig' %}
{% import 'config/maintenance/_macros.html.twig' as m %}

{% block maintenance_title %}Sauvegardes récentes{% endblock %}

{% block maintenance_content %}
    {# ————— Sauvegardes récentes —————

       One list sorted by date, families mixed: one looks here for « the
       most recent », never for « the scheduled ones ». The family is a
       pill on the row, not a grouping.

       Five rows, then the rest behind a Bootstrap « collapse »: exactly
       the mechanism the update history uses, with the same
       collapse-label.js. Two ways of folding a list would be one too
       many, and the changing label comes from the script because a CSS
       swap fails while the service worker still serves the old
       stylesheet (see that file). #}
    <div class="card mb-4" id="maintenance-backups-list">
        <div class="card-body">
            {{ m.section_header('maintenance-backups-list-body', 'Sauvegardes récentes', true) }}
            <div class="collapse show mt-3" id="maintenance-backups-list-body">
                {% if backups is empty %}
                    {% include 'partials/empty_state.html.twig' with {
                        message: 'Aucune sauvegarde pour le moment.',
                        compact: true,
                    } only %}
                {% else %}
                    {{ m.backup_rows(backups|slice(0, backups_shown_at_once)) }}
                    {% if backups|length > backups_shown_at_once %}
                        <div class="collapse" id="backups-more">
                            {{ m.backup_rows(backups|slice(backups_shown_at_once)) }}
                        </div>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm mt-2 collapsed"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#backups-more"
                                aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="backups-more"
                                data-collapse-label-expanded="Réduire">
                            <span data-collapse-label>Voir plus ({{ backups|length - backups_shown_at_once }})</span>
                            <i class="bi bi-chevron-down ms-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        </button>
                    {% endif %}
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    {# ————— Restaurer une sauvegarde —————

       Moved here from the red « Réinitialisation » card (issue #619,
       IT-06), carrying everything with it: both sources, the chunked
       upload of a large archive, portable archives kept out of the
       server list, the RESTAURER keyword, and the safety backup taken
       first. What changed is the password: an archive of this server
       needs none, so the field only appears for an uploaded file. #}
    <div class="card mb-4" id="maintenance-restore">
        <div class="card-body">
            {{ m.section_header('maintenance-restore-body', 'Restaurer une sauvegarde', true) }}
            <div class="collapse show mt-3" id="maintenance-restore-body">
                <p class="text-body-secondary small">
                    Restaure la base de données et les fichiers depuis une sauvegarde existante ou un fichier
                    téléversé. Une sauvegarde de sécurité est prise automatiquement avant la restauration.
                </p>
                <p class="small text-warning-emphasis">
                    <i class="bi bi-key"></i>
                    Une archive ne contient <strong>pas les clés de chiffrement</strong> : elle ne se relit
                    que sur l'installation qui l'a produite, ou sur une installation dont
                    <code>storage/keys/</code> et <code>storage/config/</code> ont été recopiés depuis
                    celle-là.
                </p>
                <form id="restore-backup-form" method="post" action="/config/maintenance/reset/restore" enctype="multipart/form-data">
                    {{ csrf_field()|raw }}
                    {# Set by maintenance.js after a large archive has been
                       sent as chunks (audit M2); the classic POST then
                       references the assembled file instead of carrying it. #}
                    <input type="hidden" name="upload_id" id="restore-upload-id" value="">

                    <div class="mb-2">
                        <div class="form-check">
                            <input class="form-check-input" type="radio" name="source" id="restore-source-server" value="server" checked>
                            <label class="form-check-label small" for="restore-source-server">Depuis le serveur</label>
                        </div>
                        <div class="form-check">
                            <input class="form-check-input" type="radio" name="source" id="restore-source-upload" value="upload">
                            <label class="form-check-label small" for="restore-source-upload">Depuis un fichier téléversé</label>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="mb-2" id="restore-server-picker">
                        <label class="visually-hidden" for="restore-backup-id">Sauvegarde à restaurer</label>
                        <select class="form-select form-select-sm" name="backup_id" id="restore-backup-id" {% if backups is empty %}disabled{% endif %}>
                            {# `not backup.isPortable`: a portable archive is for starting
                               over on a NEW installation, not for
                               overwriting this one. Offering it here
                               would lead to a destructive restore
                               followed by a rollback, for an operation
                               that cannot succeed — the controller
                               refuses it too, and it is what counts;
                               this only spares finding that out. #}
                            {% for backup in backups %}
                                {% if backup.status == 'completed' and not backup.isPortable %}
                                    <option value="{{ backup.id }}"{% if backup.needsTypedPassword %} data-needs-password="1"{% endif %}>{{ backup.typeLabel }} — {{ backup.createdAt }}</option>
                                {% endif %}
                            {% endfor %}
                        </select>
                    </div>
                    <div class="mb-2 d-none" id="restore-upload-picker">
                        <input type="file" class="form-control form-control-sm" name="backup_file" id="restore-backup-file" accept=".zip" aria-label="Fichier de sauvegarde">
                    </div>
                    <div class="mb-2 d-none" id="restore-password-field">
                        {# One field for both: the password of an
                           encrypted full backup, or the passphrase of a
                           portable one. The site tells which it received
                           from the archive's own header, so asking the
                           same thing twice in two fields would only make
                           the operator choose between them.

                           Hidden for an archive of this server since issue
                           #619 (IT-06): the site restores it with the
                           password it kept. maintenance.js shows it for an
                           uploaded file, and for the one archive of this
                           server whose password was never kept — a full
                           backup from before IT-03, flagged on its option. #}
                        {% include 'partials/form_field.html.twig' with {
                            field_id: 'restore-backup-password', field_name: 'password',
                            type: 'password', label: "Mot de passe ou phrase de passe de l'archive",
                            help: "Pour une sauvegarde venue d'ailleurs, ou une sauvegarde complète de ce serveur antérieure aux mots de passe générés. Les autres sauvegardes de ce serveur n'en demandent pas : le site connaît le leur.",
                            size: 'sm', wrapper_class: '',
                        } only %}
                    </div>
                    <label class="form-label small" for="restore-backup-keyword">Tapez <strong>RESTAURER</strong> pour confirmer</label>
                    <input type="text" class="form-control form-control-sm mb-2" name="confirm_keyword" id="restore-backup-keyword" autocomplete="off">
                    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-outline-danger btn-sm" id="restore-backup-submit" disabled>
                        Restaurer
                    </button>
                    <output class="mt-2 small d-none d-block" id="restore-backup-progress"><span class="spinner-border spinner-border-sm"></span> Restauration en cours…</output>
                    <div class="mt-2 small text-danger d-none" id="restore-backup-error" role="alert"></div>
                </form>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
